CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ converting fixed param, template viable: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [over.match.funcs]/[over.ics.user]: a function template with a fixed
class-type parameter S is viable when the argument is convertible to S via a
user-defined conversion (const char* -> S).  CBMC's post-deduction compatibility
check dropped the candidate whenever the argument was not itself a class type;
fixed to reject only when no implicit conversion sequence exists.  This is the
util/invariant.h report_invariant_failure(const std::string&,...) shape.
assertion.2 provides non-vacuity.
